{:event/id "ea160ffc-df58-4b00-9332-778e1b26f50d" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:4571709a-0033-48d1-9011-0c8d16fd59fc" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["4571709a-0033-48d1-9011-0c8d16fd59fc"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:4571709a-0033-48d1-9011-0c8d16fd59fc" :event/at "2026-09-08T14:01:01Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/auth-state-is-ephemeral-one-shot-nonce :finding/shapes #{:cell :lifecycle :scope :infra} :finding/current-name "auth.session pending-states + create-state/consume-state" :finding/candidate-name "EphemeralOneShotNonce<Token,Context>" :finding/claim "Knoxx GitHub OAuth state is a process-local map entry keyed by a random token and carrying redirect context plus creation time. Creation opportunistically prunes old entries; consumption removes the entry before checking the TTL and returns it only while live. The proven law is one-shot consumption within one process plus expiry, not durable reservation, replay authority, or cross-process atomic claim."}}
{:event/id "c7fd79f8-5958-43e7-831c-f03126576728" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:4571709a-0033-48d1-9011-0c8d16fd59fc" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["ea160ffc-df58-4b00-9332-778e1b26f50d"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:4571709a-0033-48d1-9011-0c8d16fd59fc" :event/at "2026-09-08T14:01:01Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/mcp-code-is-bound-one-shot-grant :finding/shapes #{:store :claim :capability :law} :finding/current-name "mongo-mcp-oauth peek-code!/consume-code! + MCP token exchange" :finding/candidate-name "BoundOneShotGrant<Token,Binding>" :finding/claim "MCP authorization codes are durable expiring grants with an explicit validate-before-consume law. The route first peeks without spending the code, validates client, redirect, and PKCE bindings, then atomically claims it with find-one-and-delete; concurrent otherwise-valid exchanges may both pass validation but exactly one claim wins, and the credential minted downstream uses the claimed record rather than the earlier peek. Missing or unreadable expiry fails closed. This is stronger than an ephemeral nonce and distinct from ReservationGate because consumption is terminal rather than an in-flight claim state."}}
{:event/id "af37ae86-a8b4-4e5e-abcd-d07ec6771afa" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:4571709a-0033-48d1-9011-0c8d16fd59fc" :event/seq 3 :event/causes ["c7fd79f8-5958-43e7-831c-f03126576728"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:4571709a-0033-48d1-9011-0c8d16fd59fc" :event/at "2026-09-08T14:01:01Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/invite-redemption-does-not-prove-bound-one-shot-law :finding/shapes #{:store :domain-algorithm :claim :counterexample} :finding/current-name "mongo-policy-invites pending-by-code!/redeem-invite! + policy/redeem-invite!" :finding/candidate-name "RedeemableInvite<Code,Subject> (counterexample)" :finding/claim "Invite redemption looks superficially like another one-shot credential but does not satisfy BoundOneShotGrant at the inspected store seam. The policy layer reads a pending non-expired invite, checks the email, and later updates by invite_id; the store update does not predicate on pending status or atomically return a single winner. This does not prove duplicate user creation succeeds elsewhere; it proves only that invite storage itself does not establish the exactly-one consumption law and therefore should not be compressed into the stronger grant abstraction on naming similarity alone."}}
